    <entry xml:lang="en">
        <title>Baldurwind</title>
        <published>2024-04-13T00:00:00+00:00</published>
        <updated>2024-04-13T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
        
        <author>
          <name>
            
              Unknown
            
          </name>
        </author>
        
        <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://DreamWeave-MP.github.io/S3ctors-S3cret-St4sh/baldurwind/"/>
        <id>https://DreamWeave-MP.github.io/S3ctors-S3cret-St4sh/baldurwind/</id>
        
        <summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;Baldurwind is a mechanical total conversion for OpenMW. More features are planned, but in essence, Baldurwind&#x27;s goal is to convert Morrowind into turn-based, party RPG!&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The idea was inspired due to the sheer popularity of Baldur&#x27;s Gate 3 (obviously) and some of my longstanding grievances with the combat system. There&#x27;s not enough audiovisual feedback in typical Morrowind combat, so instead of removing hit chance (as I did in another mod), I designed some mechanics which enable the game to (in my opinion) more properly lean into that idea.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;</summary>
        
    </entry>
